{
  "video": {
    "id": "SvjeCxVu2dI",
    "title": "Genomic and cDNA Libraries | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SvjeCxVu2dI",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 249,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 86,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.8100000000000005,
      "end": 9.02,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Hello, and welcome to another help session on"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 9.02,
      "end": 10.27,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "recombinant DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.27,
      "end": 11.96,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "Today we're going to discuss genomic"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 11.96,
      "end": 14.29,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "libraries and cDNA libraries."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 14.29,
      "end": 16.1,
      "duration": 1.81,
      "text": "So what is a genomic library?"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 16.1,
      "end": 19.34,
      "duration": 3.24,
      "text": "Well, with most organisms the genome is really too"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 19.34,
      "end": 20.08,
      "duration": 0.74,
      "text": "large to deal with."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 20.08,
      "end": 22.26,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "It's too large to work with or to examine."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 22.26,
      "end": 24.87,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "So oftentimes it's more useful to cut it down into smaller"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 24.87,
      "end": 27.6,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "pieces that you can then examine."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 27.6,
      "end": 29.17,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "How do we make a genomic library?"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 29.17,
      "end": 32.92,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "Well, we start off with our cell of interest."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 32.92,
      "end": 34.75,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "And the first thing that we're going to do is we're going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 34.75,
      "end": 37.94,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "isolate all the DNA from the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 37.94,
      "end": 40.51,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "Once we have the DNA, we're going to use restriction"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 40.51,
      "end": 43.5,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "enzymes to cut it into smaller sections."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 43.5,
      "end": 45.65,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "Now, we have to be very careful when we choose which"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 45.65,
      "end": 47.72,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "restriction enzyme we want to use."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 47.72,
      "end": 51.24,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "We want to use an enzyme that has enough restriction sites"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 51.24,
      "end": 53.94,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "in the genome so that we'll get small enough pieces to put"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 53.94,
      "end": 56.58,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "in the vector, but not so small that all the"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 56.58,
      "end": 59.96,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "genes get cut up."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 59.96,
      "end": 62.25,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "Usually what we we'll use for the vector is a plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 62.25,
      "end": 65.53,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "A plasmid is a very standard and easy way to get foreign"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 65.53,
      "end": 68.03,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "DNA into a bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 68.03,
      "end": 71.44,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "So we're going to cut up our DNA and the plasmid with our"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 71.44,
      "end": 72.9,
      "duration": 1.46,
      "text": "restriction enzyme."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 72.9,
      "end": 75.39,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "Sometimes we might want to even make two different"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 75.39,
      "end": 78.83,
      "duration": 3.44,
      "text": "libraries using two different restriction enzymes so that"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 78.83,
      "end": 80.125,
      "duration": 1.295,
      "text": "we'll have the cuts in different places."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 82.72,
      "end": 86.51,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "Once we have our cut up DNA and our plasmids, now we need"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 86.51,
      "end": 88.19,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "to ligate them together using DNA ligase."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 90.79,
      "end": 95.18,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "Once the cDNA is pasted into the plasmid, now we're ready"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 95.18,
      "end": 98.79,
      "duration": 3.61,
      "text": "to actually transform them into bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 98.79,
      "end": 101.62,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "It's very easy to transform plasmids into bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 101.62,
      "end": 102.99,
      "duration": 1.37,
      "text": "There are multiple different ways to do it."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 102.99,
      "end": 106.11,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "One common one is to use heat shock, whereby you heat the"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 106.11,
      "end": 109.15,
      "duration": 3.04,
      "text": "bacteria up and then cool it down rapidly, which causes"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 109.15,
      "end": 110.91,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "little holes to open up that allows the"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 110.91,
      "end": 114.19,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "plasmids to be taken up."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 114.19,
      "end": 117.38,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "What we end up with are thousands of different"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 117.38,
      "end": 121.28,
      "duration": 3.9,
      "text": "bacteria cells, all with different sections of the DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 121.28,
      "end": 125.17,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "So combined, all these different sections form the"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 125.17,
      "end": 127.44,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "genome, the original genome that we have, but they're in"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 127.44,
      "end": 128.6,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "much smaller sections."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 128.6,
      "end": 130.43,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "They're much easier to work with."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 130.43,
      "end": 134.35,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "And this combination of all these different cells forms"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 134.35,
      "end": 136.59,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "our genomic library."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 136.59,
      "end": 138.47,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "So that's one type of library."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 138.47,
      "end": 141.32,
      "duration": 2.85,
      "text": "Another type of library is a cDNA library."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 141.32,
      "end": 143.69,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "So the way that the cDNA library is different from a"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 143.69,
      "end": 146.69,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "genomic library is that while the genomic library"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 146.69,
      "end": 151.09,
      "duration": 4.4,
      "text": "encompasses the entire genome of the cell, the cDNA library"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 151.09,
      "end": 154.86,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "just looks at what genes are being expressed in the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 154.86,
      "end": 159.87,
      "duration": 5.01,
      "text": "So let's go over how we would make a cDNA library."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 159.87,
      "end": 162.87,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "What we're going to start off with is we're going to start"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 162.87,
      "end": 165.16,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "off by isolating the mRNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 165.16,
      "end": 168.76,
      "duration": 3.6,
      "text": "So the mRNA, clearly, is the RNA that's being"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 168.76,
      "end": 169.69,
      "duration": 0.93,
      "text": "expressed in the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 169.69,
      "end": 171.69,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "This is what's ultimately-- the proteins are going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 171.69,
      "end": 174.021,
      "duration": 2.331,
      "text": "produced by the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 174.021,
      "end": 177.53,
      "duration": 3.509,
      "text": "We're then going to use reverse transcription to"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 177.53,
      "end": 179.67,
      "duration": 2.14,
      "text": "create the DNA version of the RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 179.67,
      "end": 182.75,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "This is what we're referring to, again, as the cDNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 182.75,
      "end": 187.7,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "text": "Once we have the cDNA, we then need to add restriction sites"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 187.7,
      "end": 188.643,
      "duration": 0.943,
      "text": "to the ends of them."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 188.643,
      "end": 192.49,
      "duration": 3.847,
      "text": "Remember, before we were just able to use innate restriction"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 192.49,
      "end": 193.53,
      "duration": 1.04,
      "text": "sites in the genomes."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 193.53,
      "end": 195.72,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "But for the cDNA library, we really want to"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 195.72,
      "end": 197.62,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "keep the cDNA intact."
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 197.62,
      "end": 199.05,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "We don't want to cut it up."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 199.05,
      "end": 202.63,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "So we just want to add restriction sites to the ends"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 202.63,
      "end": 204.44,
      "duration": 1.81,
      "text": "of the cDNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 204.44,
      "end": 208.19,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "Then we can treat the cDNA and the plasmids"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 208.19,
      "end": 210.55,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "with restriction enzymes."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 210.55,
      "end": 214.5,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "Once again, once they've been cut up we can use DNA ligase"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 214.5,
      "end": 219.85,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "text": "to combine the cut up plasmids and the cut up cDNA to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 219.85,
      "end": 222.93,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "complete plasmid plus cDNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 222.93,
      "end": 227.32,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "And finally, once again, we can transform our bacteria,"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 227.32,
      "end": 230.41,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "and then the combination of all these cells, all with"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 230.41,
      "end": 234.3,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "different types of cDNA, form our cDNA library."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 234.3,
      "end": 237.24,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "And cDNA libraries are very useful if you want to compare"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 237.24,
      "end": 239.78,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "the difference in protein expressions between two"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 239.78,
      "end": 242.01,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "different cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 242.01,
      "end": 242.78,
      "duration": 0.77,
      "text": "Thank you very much."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 242.78,
      "end": 245.88,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "This has been another help session for recombinant DNA."
    }
  ],
